  "id": "Compound::DB01159 - Gene::2741",
  "verbalization": "Halothane appears to interact with Glra1 through a shared mechanism involving the GABA-A receptor subunit Gabrb3. The evidence suggests that Halothane binds to Gabrb3, which then participates in transmitter-gated ion channel activity, ultimately leading to the participation of Glra1. This indicates a potential pathway where Halothane influences Glra1 through a common intermediate, Gabrb3, by modulating GABA-A receptor function. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with some variation in the strength of the evidence across different paths. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for Halothane in modulating GABA-A receptor activity, potentially through interactions with Gabrb3 and its downstream effects on Glra1.",
